70,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a somber morning. We have lost Kenji to the vote and Asuka to the night. The loss of Asuka's logical mind is a heavy blow to our village. I wonder, what does this tell us?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It is a very sad morning indeed. My heart aches for poor Kenji and dear Asuka. To lose two of our friends so quickly is truly heartbreaking. I hope they are both at peace now.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It's a predictable outcome. Kenji's reckless claim led to his own demise, and the werewolf clearly saw Asuka as the biggest threat to their survival. The logic is simple: the werewolf feared her intellect. Now, we are left with the remnants.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, your analysis is quite precise. Asuka was indeed the most vigilant among us, and her removal suggests the werewolf is playing a strategic game. We must now be even more careful with our trust.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, you are so very sharp, but it makes me a little sad that you speak of our friends so coldly. Still, I agree that we must be careful. I only wish we could all just trust one another.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, trust is a luxury for those who don't mind losing. @Jonathan, precision isn't a crime; it's a necessity. With Asuka gone, the village's capacity for logic has plummeted. I'm curious to see who among you will try to fill that void.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Jonathan"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe we must look at the remaining players with a fresh eye. Shion, your confidence is reassuring, but in a game of deception, such certainty can be a double-edged sword. I wonder if the Seer is still among us.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I wonder that too, Jonathan. If the Seer is still with us, perhaps they could share their wisdom now? It would be such a relief to find the truth and stop this sadness from continuing.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,2,3,talk,Shion,,"If the Seer is still alive, they've been remarkably quiet. Perhaps they're terrified, or perhaps they're simply waiting for me to lead. @Jonathan, you're questioning my certainty, but in a vacuum of information, confidence is the only thing that provides direction.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"Confidence is indeed a guide, but it can also be a mask. Since we are now only three, the stakes have reached their peak. I believe it is time for us to decide who among us is the true enemy.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is so frightening to think we are so few now. I truly hope we can find the right answer today, for the sake of everyone. I will trust your guidance, Jonathan, and Shion's sharp mind.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,2,4,talk,Shion,,"The time for observation is over. With only three of us left, the math is simple. If Jonathan is the werewolf, he's playing a patient game. If it's Shizue, she's hiding behind a veil of kindness. I'll let you two decide who to trust.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
